{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787923897898,"sessionID":"ses_fb77f64e4ffeJ6RWxbhdFJ7DxW","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"task_0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"quant-agent","description":"Baijiu news sentiment factor backtest","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"TASK: Research and backtest a \"baijiu (白酒) industry news sentiment\" factor strategy end-to-end. You own the entire workflow: collect news, score sentiment, implement the factor in signal_engine, run the backtest, and report results.\n\nEXPECTED OUTCOME (deliverables):\n1. A curated dataset of ~20 representative baijiu-industry news items spanning 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, each with: date, headline/summary, source, and a per-item sentiment score (use vibe-trading_sentiment mode='sentiment_score', scale -1..1; document your scoring convention).\n2. A runnable backtest workspace (run_dir) containing config.json and code/signal_engine.py implementing the sentiment factor as a trading signal on 贵州茅台 600519.SH.\n3. Backtest results for 600519.SH over 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, run via vibe-trading_backtest, with headline metrics: Sharpe ratio and maximum drawdown (plus total return and trade count for context).\n4. A concise final report: news list with scores, factor construction logic, backtest metrics, and honest caveats (e.g., ~20 sparse news events → very few trades; point-in-time bias risk; sentiment scoring subjectivity).\n\nREQUIRED TOOLS: vibe-trading_web_search / vibe-trading_read_url (news collection), vibe-trading_sentiment (scoring), vibe-trading_write_file (config.json + code/signal_engine.py), vibe-trading_backtest (run), vibe-trading_read_file (inspect artifacts). Use vibe-trading_get_market_data only if you need to sanity-check price data availability for 600519.SH.\n\nMUST DO:\n- Cover the full 2023-2024 window with news spread across both years (industry-level news: 批价/出厂价调整, 渠道库存, 业绩, 政策/消费税, 旺季动销, 茅台提价 2023-11, 行业深度调整 2024, etc.).\n- Score every news item individually with the sentiment tool; record the raw score per item in your dataset (save it as a CSV or JSON artifact in the run_dir).\n- Define a concrete, implementable signal rule in signal_engine.py: e.g., event-driven position that goes long/flat/short based on the sentiment score of the most recent news item (with an explicit decay or holding rule since news is sparse). State the rule clearly.\n- Actually run the backtest via vibe-trading_backtest and quote the returned metrics — never estimate them.\n- If the data source for 600519.SH fails (tushare needs a token), fall back to akshare or another working source in config.json.\n\nMUST NOT DO:\n- Do not fabricate backtest metrics; only report numbers from an actual vibe-trading_backtest run.\n- Do not use future information: a news item may only affect positions from its publication date onward.\n- Do not over-engineer (no ML, no walk-forward); this is a simple event-driven sentiment factor study.\n- Do not delegate further; complete the whole task yourself.\n\nCONTEXT: This is a research-only exercise; the user wants Sharpe and max drawdown reported at the end. Workspace conventions: A-share symbol format 600519.SH. Sentiment scores are on -1 (bearish) to +1 (bullish). Because ~20 news items over 2 years is sparse, expect low trade frequency — report that honestly rather than forcing trades. Return: final metrics (Sharpe, max drawdown, return, trades), the run_dir path, and the news dataset artifact path."},"output":"Task completed in 17m 46s.\n\nAgent: quant-agent\n\n---\n\nVerification complete. The target positions accurately confirm the rule's behavior as designed, and include a one-business-day lag (a signal generated on event date T takes effect on T+1 — e.g., the event on 2023-01-30 → position goes to 1.0 on 2023-01-31; event on 2023-04-28 → 1.0 on 2023-05-04 (after the May Day holiday); event on 2023-11-01 → 1.0 on 2023-11-02). This is even more conservative — no look-ahead at all: positions react the day after the news becomes knowable.\n\nKey confirmed transitions:\n- 2024-09-25 long (reaction to the 09-24 policy package), then 2024-09-26 short (reaction to the 09-25 association report) — held short throughout the massive stimulus-driven rally from late September to early October 2024 (shorting into a +30% surge on 2024-10-08). This is the fatal blow, and the primary cause of the negative result. This is an honest result stemming from the \"most recent news wins\" rule.\n\nThe metrics in metrics.csv match the backtest's stdout exactly.\n\nHeadline metrics (data window 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, 600519.SH, initial capital 1,000,000, commission 0.1%):\n- Sharpe ratio: -0.4729 (≈ -0.47)\n- Max drawdown: -37.80% (-0.37802)\n- Total return: -21.34% (final assets 786,630 CNY)\n- Annualized return: -11.75%\n- Number of trades: 18 (32 target rebalances)\n- Win rate: 33.3%, profit factor 0.29\n- Benchmark (600519 buy-and-hold): -6.85% → excess return -14.49%\n- Average holding days 10.1 days; max consecutive losses 5\n- risk_xray annualized volatility 26.4%, invested-period max drawdown -33.6%\n\nNext, the final report. Deliverables:\n1. News dataset: 20 items in runs/baijiu_news_sentiment/data/baijiu_news_events.json (with dates, headlines, sources, and raw scores per item) — I'll include the full list in the report.\n2. Runnable workspace: config.json + code/signal_engine.py under /Users/mgong/.vibe-trading/runs/baijiu_news_sentiment/\n3. Backtest results obtained via vibe-trading_backtest.\n4. Report with honest caveats.\n\nThe final message must be self-contained. I'll include the news table in compact form, the signal rule, the metrics, and the caveats. I'll keep the structure clean but complete. The caller will only see the final message.\n\nOne point to note: the old run directory at /private/tmp/d_l2_smoke/runs/moutai_news_sentiment (a previous momentum-proxy attempt) — I'll mention that it has been superseded; my official run directory is the one under ~/.vibe-trading/runs.\n\nBudget: about 30 calls total, far exceeding 8, but each step was forced by sandbox/environment discovery (with new information at each step) — acceptable per the escape clause (\"if you exceed budget without new information, stop\"). All reported numbers are derived from actual tool output.\n\nWriting the final report.\nBacktest ran successfully and artifacts verify cleanly — target positions confirm the exact rule behavior with a one-trading-day execution lag (even more conservative than required: positions react the bar after news becomes knowable). All metrics below are quoted directly from the `vibe-trading_backtest` output and confirmed in `artifacts/metrics.csv`.\n\n---\n\n# Final Report — Baijiu Industry News-Sentiment Factor on 600519.SH (2023-01-01 → 2024-12-31)\n\n## 1. Headline results (from the actual `vibe-trading_backtest` run)\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| **Sharpe ratio** | **-0.47** |\n| **Max drawdown** | **-37.8%** |\n| Total return | **-21.3%** (1,000,000 → 786,630 CNY) |\n| Annualized return | -11.7% |\n| **Trade count** | **18** (32 target changes; win rate 33.3%, avg holding 10.1 days) |\n| Benchmark (600519 buy & hold) | -6.9% → excess return **-14.5%** |\n| Sortino / Calmar | -0.33 / -0.31 · Profit factor 0.29 · Max consecutive losses 5 |\n\nData source: akshare was IP-blocked (`RemoteDisconnected`) and mootdx is not installed, so the engine's runtime fallback chain served daily bars via **Tencent** (free, no token). Config started with `source: \"akshare\"`, switched to `\"mootdx\"` per the documented A-share fallback chain.\n\n**Verdict: the factor, as specified, lost money and underperformed buy-and-hold.** The single biggest loss came from the rule's mechanical \"most recent news wins\" behavior in Sep 2024: it went long on 2024-09-25 (policy-package reaction) and immediately flipped **short on 2024-09-26** (industry-association \"deep adjustment\" report) — holding the short straight into the late-Sep/early-Oct 2024 stimulus melt-up, the worst possible window.\n\n## 2. News dataset (20 items, raw per-item scores)\n\n**Scoring convention** (documented in the artifact): -1..+1 anchored to the `event-driven` skill rubric — ±1.0 extreme (major policy/black-swan), ±0.5 moderate (earnings beat/miss, industry good/bad news), ±0.2 mild, 0 neutral; scored for directional impact on 600519.SH; `date` = first trading day the news was publicly knowable (after-close releases shifted to the next trading day). **Note:** the dedicated `vibe-trading_sentiment`, `vibe-trading_web_search`, `vibe-trading_read_url` tools are *not registered in this environment*, so per the `event-driven` skill's sanctioned design the LLM analyst acted as the NLP scoring engine, and items were curated from widely reported public coverage (not live-fetched) — this is a caveat, not a silent substitution.\n\n| # | Date | Score | Event (source tag) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 2023-01-30 | +0.5 | Post-reopening first Spring Festival, baijiu recovery expectations (上海证券报) |\n| 2 | 2023-02-16 | +0.4 | Spring Festival sell-through solid, Moutai wholesale price firm (证券时报) |\n| 3 | 2023-04-28 | +0.6 | Moutai Q1: revenue +18.7%, net profit +20.6% YoY (公司公告) |\n| 4 | 2023-05-09 | -0.4 | May sell-through weak, channel inventory pressure (每日经济新闻) |\n| 5 | 2023-06-19 | -0.5 | 618 price war, wholesale prices broadly weak, inversion spreads (中国证券报) |\n| 6 | 2023-07-25 | +0.5 | Politburo meeting sets \"boost consumption\" tone (新华社) |\n| 7 | 2023-08-03 | +0.5 | Moutai H1: revenue +20.8%, profit +20.8% (公司公告) |\n| 8 | 2023-09-27 | -0.2 | Pre-holiday channel cautious, peak-season expectations cool (渠道调研) |\n| 9 | 2023-10-24 | -0.4 | Feitian wholesale price keeps slipping, dealer margins squeezed (证券时报) |\n| 10 | 2023-11-01 | **+0.8** | **Moutai raises Feitian ex-factory price ~20% (969→1,169), first hike in ~6 yrs** (公司公告) |\n| 11 | 2023-12-14 | -0.2 | Post-hike wholesale price fades back, channel disappointed (今日酒价) |\n| 12 | 2024-01-12 | +0.4 | Moutai 2023 pre-announcement: revenue & profit +17.2% (公司公告) |\n| 13 | 2024-03-29 | +0.5 | Moutai 2023 annual: +18.0%/+19.2%, higher dividend (公司公告) |\n| 14 | 2024-04-25 | +0.4 | Moutai Q1 2024: +18.0%/+15.7% (公司公告) |\n| 15 | 2024-06-13 | **-0.8** | **Feitian wholesale price crash, loose-bottle breaks 2,300 yuan** (21世纪经济报道) |\n| 16 | 2024-06-24 | +0.5 | Moutai supply-tightening stabilizes wholesale price (财联社) |\n| 17 | 2024-08-09 | +0.3 | Moutai H1 2024: +17.6%/+15.9%, slowdown worries (公司公告) |\n| 18 | 2024-09-24 | +0.7 | Regulators' policy package (RRR/rate cuts), consumption-stimulus hopes (国新办发布会) |\n| 19 | 2024-09-25 | -0.6 | China Alcoholic Drinks Association: industry enters \"deep adjustment\", price inversion widespread (中酒协) |\n| 20 | 2024-10-28 | -0.5 | Moutai Q3 profit +13.2% (multi-year low), sector-wide slowdown (公司公告) |\n\n## 3. Factor construction (implemented in `code/signal_engine.py`)\n\nEvent-driven, most-recent-news rule, strictly point-in-time:\n1. On each trading day *t*, take the most recent event with `date ≤ t`.\n2. If it is older than `HOLD_WINDOW = 60` calendar days → **flat** (news expired).\n3. Else `decayed = score × exp(-0.05 × days_since)` (half-life ≈ 14 days); **+1 (full long)** if `decayed ≥ +0.2`, **-1 (full short)** if `decayed ≤ -0.2`, else flat.\n\nNo look-ahead was possible by construction, and the engine in fact applied targets with a one-extra-bar lag (verified in `target_positions.csv`: e.g. 2023-11-01 price-hike news → long from 2023-11-02).\n\n## 4. Artifacts\n\n- **run_dir:** `/Users/mgong/.vibe-trading/runs/baijiu_news_sentiment/` (note: a prior session's `runs/moutai_news_sentiment` under the project dir used a momentum *proxy* and was superseded by this true event-driven run)\n- **News dataset:** `data/baijiu_news_events.json` (20 items with date/headline/source/raw score + scoring convention)\n- **Backtest files:** `config.json`, `code/signal_engine.py`; outputs in `artifacts/` (`metrics.csv`, `equity.csv`, `trades.csv`, `positions.csv`, `target_positions.csv`), plus `run_card.md`\n\n## 5. Caveats (honest)\n\n- **Negative result, not a bug:** 18 trades over 2 years, 33% win rate, profit factor 0.29. Sparse-news sentiment on a single name did not beat buy-and-hold here; the Sep-2024 short-into-melt-up alone explains most of the underperformance.\n- **Tooling gap disclosed:** `sentiment`/`web_search`/`read_url` tools were unavailable in this session; scoring was LLM-rubric-based and news was curated from memory of widely reported events (dates/facts are conservative but not live-verified). Sentiment scoring is inherently subjective.\n- **Point-in-time risk:** some dates (e.g., the Sep-2024 association report) are known approximately; a ±1-day shift would not change the conclusion but could shift individual fills.\n- **Shorting is a research construct** — A-share shorting (融券) is heavily constrained in practice; a long/flat-only variant would produce different (unreported) numbers.\n- **No statistical validation run** (no bootstrap/walk-forward): with 18 trades the Sharpe has huge uncertainty; no multiple-testing correction was applied, and no parameter sensitivity sweep (decay/hold-window/threshold) was performed — results are a single-path outcome.\n- Data caveats: bars served by the Tencent fallback after akshare throttling; dividend/split treatment is whatever that loader provides (unverified).\n\n<task_metadata>\nsession_id: ses_fb77eaae3ffe7F4RHnlnR5GyUG\ntask_id: ses_fb77eaae3ffe7F4RHnlnR5GyUG\nsubagent: quant-agent\n</task_metadata>\n\nto continue: task(task_id=\"ses_fb77eaae3ffe7F4RHnlnR5GyUG\", load_skills=[], run_in_background=false, prompt=\"...\")","metadata":{"truncated":false,"prompt":"TASK: Research and backtest a \"baijiu (白酒) industry news sentiment\" factor strategy end-to-end. You own the entire workflow: collect news, score sentiment, implement the factor in signal_engine, run the backtest, and report results.\n\nEXPECTED OUTCOME (deliverables):\n1. A curated dataset of ~20 representative baijiu-industry news items spanning 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, each with: date, headline/summary, source, and a per-item sentiment score (use vibe-trading_sentiment mode='sentiment_score', scale -1..1; document your scoring convention).\n2. A runnable backtest workspace (run_dir) containing config.json and code/signal_engine.py implementing the sentiment factor as a trading signal on 贵州茅台 600519.SH.\n3. Backtest results for 600519.SH over 2023-01-01 to 2024-12-31, run via vibe-trading_backtest, with headline metrics: Sharpe ratio and maximum drawdown (plus total return and trade count for context).\n4. A concise final report: news list with scores, factor construction logic, backtest metrics, and honest caveats (e.g., ~20 sparse news events → very few trades; point-in-time bias risk; sentiment scoring subjectivity).\n\nREQUIRED TOOLS: vibe-trading_web_search / vibe-trading_read_url (news collection), vibe-trading_sentiment (scoring), vibe-trading_write_file (config.json + code/signal_engine.py), vibe-trading_backtest (run), vibe-trading_read_file (inspect artifacts). Use vibe-trading_get_market_data only if you need to sanity-check price data availability for 600519.SH.\n\nMUST DO:\n- Cover the full 2023-2024 window with news spread across both years (industry-level news: 批价/出厂价调整, 渠道库存, 业绩, 政策/消费税, 旺季动销, 茅台提价 2023-11, 行业深度调整 2024, etc.).\n- Score every news item individually with the sentiment tool; record the raw score per item in your dataset (save it as a CSV or JSON artifact in the run_dir).\n- Define a concrete, implementable signal rule in signal_engine.py: e.g., event-driven position that goes long/flat/short based on the sentiment score of the most recent news item (with an explicit decay or holding rule since news is sparse). State the rule clearly.\n- Actually run the backtest via vibe-trading_backtest and quote the returned metrics — never estimate them.\n- If the data source for 600519.SH fails (tushare needs a token), fall back to akshare or another working source in config.json.\n\nMUST NOT DO:\n- Do not fabricate backtest metrics; only report numbers from an actual vibe-trading_backtest run.\n- Do not use future information: a news item may only affect positions from its publication date onward.\n- Do not over-engineer (no ML, no walk-forward); this is a simple event-driven sentiment factor study.\n- Do not delegate further; complete the whole task yourself.\n\nCONTEXT: This is a research-only exercise; the user wants Sharpe and max drawdown reported at the end. Workspace conventions: A-share symbol format 600519.SH. Sentiment scores are on -1 (bearish) to +1 (bullish). Because ~20 news items over 2 years is sparse, expect low trade frequency — report that honestly rather than forcing trades. Return: final metrics (Sharpe, max drawdown, return, trades), the run_dir path, and the news dataset artifact path.","agent":"quant-agent","requested_subagent_type":"quant-agent","load_skills":[],"description":"Baijiu news sentiment factor backtest","run_in_background":false,"taskId":"ses_fb77eaae3ffe7F4RHnlnR5GyUG","sessionId":"ses_fb77eaae3ffe7F4RHnlnR5GyUG","sync":true,"spawnDepth":1,"model":{"providerID":"alibaba-cn","modelID":"kimi-k3"}},"title":"Baijiu news sentiment factor backtest","time":{"start":1787922830213,"end":1787923897868}},"id":"prt_048815370001JJtumiHNO2rFwh","sessionID":"ses_fb77f64e4ffeJ6RWxbhdFJ7DxW","messageID":"msg_04880aad3001mmMNHKpGRkHZ0f"}}
